# Configuration for /etc/init.d/obscura
# Shared verbatim with net-vpn/obscura; keep the two copies byte-identical.

# How the tunnel's DNS servers get installed on the system:
#   auto             use systemd-resolved if running, else NetworkManager
#   resolved         systemd-resolved only
#   network-manager  NetworkManager only (reached over D-Bus)
#   disabled         leave the system resolver alone
#
# "auto" REFUSES TO START when neither systemd-resolved nor NetworkManager is
# running ("no supported DNS manager detected").  On an OpenRC box that
# manages networking with netifrc, dhcpcd or iwd alone, set "disabled":
# the tunnel still comes up, but DNS keeps using whatever /etc/resolv.conf
# names, so queries may leave the tunnel's DNS path.
OBSCURA_DNS="auto"

# Extra arguments for "obscura service", e.g. "-vv" for info-level logs.
# Logs are written to /var/log/obscura.
OBSCURA_OPTS=""
